      "Kamí leaves out the person spoken to; táyo includes them.",
      "Ikáw starts a sentence; ka follows the predicate.",
      "Kayó and silá are also the polite way to say you.",
      "Ay becomes 'y after a word ending in a vowel.",
      "Itó = near me, iyán = near you, iyón = far from both. Plurals take ang mga."
